---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { STEPS } from '../../data/steps';
import { PERMISSION_CATEGORIES, POLICY_OPTIONS } from '../../data/rules';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How It Works"
  description="How GenMD builds a CLAUDE.md for Claude Code, what each command permission policy means, and how your answers stay in your browser."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">How GenMD works</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-muted">
      <code class="font-mono">CLAUDE.md</code> is a file Claude Code reads at the start of a session to
      learn about your project and how you want it to work. GenMD builds one from your answers to a
      short questionnaire.
    </p>

    <section aria-labelledby="steps-heading" class="mt-12">
      <h2 id="steps-heading" class="text-xl font-bold">The six steps</h2>
      <ol class="mt-4 space-y-3">
        {
          STEPS.map((step, index) => (
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="font-semibold text-accent">{index + 1}.</span>
              <span>
                <strong class="font-semibold">{step.title}:</strong>{' '}
                <span class="text-ink-muted">{step.summary}</span>
              </span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="permissions-heading" class="mt-12">
      <h2 id="permissions-heading" class="text-xl font-bold">Command permissions</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">For each category of command, choose one policy:</p>
      <dl class="mt-4 space-y-2">
        {
          POLICY_OPTIONS.map((policy) => (
            <div>
              <dt class="inline font-semibold">{policy.label}:</dt>{' '}
              <dd class="inline text-ink-muted">{policy.description}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>

      <h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold">Categories</h3>
      <ul class="mt-3 space-y-3">
        {
          PERMISSION_CATEGORIES.map((category) => (
            <li>
              <strong class="font-semibold">{category.label}.</strong>{' '}
              <span class="text-ink-muted">{category.description}</span>
              <span class="block text-sm text-ink-subtle">
                Examples: <code class="font-mono">{category.examples}</code>
              </span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>

      <div class="mt-6 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-warn bg-warn-soft p-4" role="note">
        <p class="font-semibold text-warn-ink">Guidance, not enforcement</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-warn-ink">
          The permission rules in CLAUDE.md describe how you want Claude to behave. They do not technically
          block any command. To enforce them, configure Claude Code's permission settings as well (for
          example, the <code class="font-mono">permissions</code> section of <code class="font-mono">.claude/settings.json</code>).
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="privacy-heading" class="mt-12">
      <h2 id="privacy-heading" class="text-xl font-bold">Privacy</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">
        GenMD runs entirely in your browser. Your answers are kept in memory only: they are not uploaded,
        stored or shared, and they are cleared when you close or reload the page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="limitations-heading" class="mt-12">
      <h2 id="limitations-heading" class="text-xl font-bold">Limitations</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-ink-muted">
        <li>Output is built from templates. GenMD does not read or analyse your codebase.</li>
        <li>Answers are not saved between visits. Download your file before leaving the page.</li>
        <li>Review the generated file before using it, and adjust anything that does not fit your project.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
